#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""imp — faeOS terminal art generator.

Draws a themed TUI where you type a wish, and Imp (a local Qwen2.5 Coder on
port 8082) conjures ANSI art into a pink ✦ box. Imp's Comment — a grumpy
smollm2 haiku dragon on port 8081 — snarks about it. Every piece is saved
to ~/pixie_art/ as .txt (+ .pdf, dependency-free) and indexed in a gallery.

Usage:
  imp                          TUI (type a wish, Enter to conjure)
  imp "a moonlit mushroom"     one-shot: print art, save to gallery
  imp "prompt" --style ascii --pdf
  imp --gallery                list the gallery
  imp --demo                   render a sample frame (no server needed)

Keys in the TUI:
  Enter   conjure      a       animate (multi-frame LLM sequence, optional prompt)
  r       refine ("Make it more …")
  s       save         g       gallery (fzf)
  /       history (fzf)         Tab     cycle style
  c       clear prompt  ↑↓/jk  browse history
  ←/→     scrub frames (animated)     q/Esc   quit

Env:
  PIXIE_LLM_URL       http://127.0.0.1:8082   (imp generator)
  IMP_LLM_MODEL       alias sent to llama-server (default "imp")
  KUR_LLM_URL         http://127.0.0.1:8081   (comment dragon)
  PIXIE_MAX_TOKENS    art token budget (default 3072)
  IMP_TIMEOUT         art generation timeout, seconds (default 240)
  PIXIE_ART_DIR       save dir (default ~/pixie_art)
  PIXIE_UNICODE       1  → ✦ rounded boxes (set by default)
"""
